# API Conventions

## Responses & status codes

- `201` create (e.g. registration), `204` delete, `409` conflict (duplicate email)
- Do not return entities from controllers — use request/response DTOs
- Never expose password hashes in responses

## Error envelope

Use a global `@RestControllerAdvice`. Shape:

```json
{
  "status": 409,
  "error": "Conflict",
  "message": "An account with this email already exists",
  "timestamp": "2026-07-17T10:30:00"
}
```

Validation failures return `400` with a clear message (and field details when useful).

## Security

| Access | Endpoints |
|--------|-----------|
| Public | `/api/auth/**` |
| Authenticated | All other endpoints |

Use JWT Bearer tokens. Stateless sessions; CSRF disabled.
